t","la":12.052918,"lo":-61.754836,"d":374,"h":"Su-Th 07:00-21:00; Fr-Sa 07:00-22:00"},{"n":"St. George's Hospital","g":"essentials","k":"hospital","la":12.048279,"lo":-61.754644,"d":417},{"n":"ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":12.044727,"lo":-61.749553,"d":746,"h":"24/7"},{"n":"Port Louis Marina - Laundry","g":"essentials","k":"laundry","la":12.044474,"lo":-61.749951,"d":759},{"n":"FedEx","g":"essentials","k":"post_office","la":12.046472,"lo":-61.746347,"d":794},{"n":"Seaview Pharmacy","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":12.045893,"lo":-61.745566,"d":901,"h":"Su-Fr 08:00-20:00; Sa 09:00-20:00","ph":"14734374222"},{"n":"St. George's, Grenada","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.0525,"lo":-61.753056,"d":202,"ds":"St. George's (Grenadian Creole French: Sen Jòj) is the capital and largest city of Grenada. The city is surrounded by a hillside of an old volcano crater and is located on a horseshoe-shaped harbour.","wpu":"St. George's, Grenada","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/St_Georges_Grenada_Fort_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-St_Georges_Grenada_Fort_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Molinere Underwater Sculpture Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.08343,"lo":-61.765576,"d":3896,"ds":"The Molinere Bay Underwater Sculpture Park is a collection of ecological underwater contemporary art located in the Caribbean sea off the west coast of Grenada, West Indies and was created by British sculptor Jason deCaires Taylor. In May 2006 the world's first underwater sculpture park was opened for public viewing.","wpu":"Molinere Underwater Sculpture Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Underwater_sculptures_at_Molinere_Underwater_Sculpture_Park.jpg/960px-Underwater_sculptures_at_Molinere_Underwater_Sculpture_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Willis, Grenada","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.083333,"lo":-61.716667,"d":5261,"ds":"Willis is a town in Grenada; it is located in the Parish of Saint George, some miles inland from Saint George's, towards the center of the island. It is the community where the famous Annandale Waterfalls is eloquently situated. With lush evergreen trees, unusually- never before seen exotic plants and an array of spices and fruit trees live here.","wpu":"Willis, Grenada","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Annandale_Waterfalls.jpg/960px-Annandale_Waterfalls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hog Island (Grenada)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12,"lo":-61.738,"d":5871,"ds":"Hog Island is a small uninhabited island off the southern coast of the island of Grenada in the Caribbean. Hog Island covers 85 acres and lies 0.438 miles (0.705 km) west of Calvigny Island.","wpu":"Hog Island (Grenada)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Grenada_South_Flight_-_Hog_Island.jpg/960px-Grenada_South_Flight_-_Hog_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"St. George's (Grenadian Creole French: Sen Jòj) is the capital and largest city of Grenada. The city is surrounded by a hillside of an old volcano crater and is located on a horseshoe-shaped harbour.","wpu":"St. George's, Grenada","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/St_Georges_Grenada_Fort_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-St_Georges_Grenada_Fort_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}